{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 45,
  "title": "The war cries of monkey soldiers",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga45/kishkindhasans45.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga45/kishkindhaitrans45.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "The war cries of monkey soldiers in their enthusiasm to conquer Ravana are uttered in the audience of Sugreeva, when all of them started to their designated directions. This suggests the sugriiva aaj~na 'the inviolable order of Sugreeva.'"
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे पंच चत्वारिन्शः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 45th chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.45.1",
      "label": "4.45.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "सर्वाः च आहूय सुग्रीवः प्लवगान् प्लवगर्षभः |\nसमस्तान् च अब्रवीत् राजा राम कार्यार्थ सिद्धये\nएवम् एतत् विचेतव्यम् भवद्भिः वानरोत्तमैः |",
      "iast": "sarvāḥ ca āhūya sugrīvaḥ plavagān plavagarṣabhaḥ |\nsamastān ca abravīt rājā rāma kāryārtha siddhaye\nevam etat vicetavyam bhavadbhiḥ vānarottamaiḥ |",
      "translation": "On calling forth all the fly-jumpers for achieving the purpose of Rama's task the best fly-jumper and the king of monkeys Sugreeva spoke to all of them, \"oh, best vanara-s, you shall search all of this earth as I have detailed.\" Sugreeva said so to all monkeys.",
