      "iast": "pūrvām diśam prati yayau vinato hari yūthapaḥ\ntārā aṃgadādi sahitaḥ plavagaḥ pavanātmajaḥ |\nagastya caritām āśām dakṣiṇām hari yūthapaḥ",
      "translation": "The monkey-troop commander Vinata journeyed towards the eastern direction, and the fly-jumper, leader of monkeys and Air-god's son Hanuma travelled towards southerly quarter that is once trodden by Sage Agastya, along with Lt. Tara, Prince-regent Angada, and others.",
